---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import DiscordStory from '../components/DiscordStory.astro';
import Guide from '../components/Guide.astro';
import Mechanism from '../components/Mechanism.astro';
const chapters = ['Question', 'Save', 'Reply', 'Follow-up', 'No answer'];
const captions = [
  ['Someone asks.', 'So far, this is just a normal support thread.'],
  ['A moderator answers. Save that.', 'Right-click the reply → Apps → Save this answer.'],
  ['The question comes back.', 'Different wording. The same facts. A short, new reply.'],
  ['Then comes a follow-up.', 'The bot uses the conversation, not just the post title.'],
  ['This one is not covered.', 'The bot leaves the thread alone and queues it for a person.'],
];

---
<Base description="Save a moderator's reply. ThreadSherpa uses the saved facts to answer the next version of that question. See the conversation and the code path.">
  <section class="intro" id="top" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
    <div class="wrap intro__inner">

      <h1 id="intro-title"><span class="hero-line" data-hero-line>A Discord bot for{' '}</span><span class="hero-line hero-line--second" data-hero-line>repeat questions<span class="hero-period">.</span></span></h1>
      <div class="intro__bottom"><p data-hero-copy>A moderator answers. You save the reply.<br />The bot handles the next version of that question.</p><a class="scroll-cue" href="#how-it-works"><span>Here's the flow</span><span class="scroll-cue__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      <div class="intro-guide"><Guide pose="sleep" /></div>
      <canvas class="thread-field" data-thread-field aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="walkthrough" id="how-it-works" data-walkthrough aria-label="A support conversation, from first question to follow-up">
    <div class="story-sticky wrap">
      <div class="story-heading"><div class="story-captions">{captions.map(([title, text], index) => <div data-caption={index}><h2>{title}</h2><p>{text}</p></div>)}</div><div class="story-chapters" aria-label="Conversation steps">{chapters.map((name,index) => <button type="button" class="chapter-button" data-seek-step={index} aria-label={`Show step ${index + 1}: ${name}`} aria-current={index === 0 ? 'step' : undefined}>{name}</button>)}</div></div>
      <div class="story-composition"><div class="story-orbit" aria-hidden="true"></div><DiscordStory /><div class="memory-token" aria-hidden="true"><Guide class="story-guide" pose="idle" /><span>Answer packed.</span></div></div>
      <div class="story-bottom"><a class="text-link" href="#inside">What runs underneath <img src="/icons/arrow-right-linear.svg" width="18" height="18" alt="" /></a><button type="button" class="story-play" data-story-play hidden>Pause conversation</button></div><div class="story-track" aria-hidden="true"><span data-story-progress></span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Mechanism />

  <section class="limits-section wrap" aria-labelledby="limits-title"><div data-reveal><h2 id="limits-title">A few deliberate<br />limits.</h2></div><div class="limits-list"><details data-reveal><summary>It does not learn from every message.<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>A moderator chooses what becomes memory. A busy channel, a joke, and an unreviewed suggestion stay conversation.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>Changed rules need changed knowledge.<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Edit or remove the saved guidance. Future questions use the current facts. The bot does not broadcast corrections into old threads.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>The model can still get things wrong.<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Replies include their source so a person can check them. Unsupported questions wait. An account or payment issue needs private human support.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>You run the bot and choose the model.<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Use local Ollama inference, or Paper Instruments for replies with local embeddings. You also choose the database, support channels, and moderators.</p></details></div></section>

  <section class="project-note wrap" data-reveal><p class="project-note__text">I built this after seeing the same support questions in the MLH Discord.</p><p class="project-note__after">Different people needed the same information, but the useful answer was buried in another thread.<br /><br />Made for the <a href="https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week3-2026-10-19" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge: Week 3</a> on DEV. The theme is Slow and Steady: build something that does the work so you don't have to. This is a hackathon project, so expect rough edges. Its job is simple: let a useful moderator answer help the next person too.</p></section>

  <section class="setup-section" id="use"><div class="wrap setup-section__inner"><div class="setup-section__copy" data-reveal><h2>Run it in Discord.</h2><p>A Discord bot token. MongoDB.<br />Ollama or a Paper Instruments key.</p><a class="setup-link" href="/setup/"><span>Setup instructions</span><span class="setup-link__arrow"><img src="/icons/arrow-right-up-linear.svg" width="22" height="22" alt="" /></span></a></div><div class="setup-steps" data-reveal><ol class="setup-order"><li>Create your Discord application.</li><li>Add the environment values and start the bot.</li><li>Connect a forum. Save the first useful reply.</li></ol><div class="source-links"><a href="https://github.com/sea-deep/threadsherpa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub <img src="/icons/arrow-right-up-linear.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" /></a><a href="https://gitlab.com/wdipak/threadsherpa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitLab <img src="/icons/arrow-right-up-linear.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" /></a><a href="https://github.com/sea-deep/threadsherpa/blob/main/docs/SETUP.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quick start <img src="/icons/arrow-right-up-linear.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" /></a></div></div></div></section>
  <script>import '../scripts/afterlife';</script>
</Base>
